_answer` (§4.1, OD-PL-50). A member's patrol on another member's road rides it BY RIGHT OF THE BANNER where the receiving member believes the crown's hold `staunch` or firmer (§3.1 (f)), and otherwise crosses on THE PASSAGE's ladder, where members stand as ALLIES with the ally size tolerance (§4.7 F.3) [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r4) — RULINGS-ROUND3 §F.3 · SEAMS-r3-6: "crosses on THE PASSAGE's ladder" at every hold contradicted the banner]; PL §4.5's charter carries tolls only, so no charter carries a patrol (the brief's "by the polity-wide passage charter" is routed to the chair, `cure/D-PL-r2.md` §5). Patrols of FEUDING members clash as the feud itself, and the crown's arbitration (§6) is the remedy. Patrols stay map-only until the host's PR lights; from then the host's patrol facts go OUT through the window's three channels — each dated act (a clash, a catch, a screen, a look's report) in the events window (H9), the week just lived per road half (its presence as it was) as a lens-window row (H23) beside it, and the polity window's patrol inputs per seat (H13) — as the fold's map-side INBOX (h) ↳ and PR14 / OD-PR-36 name them. H16 is the map's INBOUND door, which the host never consumes. [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r3) — the PL-r2-verify minor ("like every other host fact" was false: the fold's (h) ↳ splits the channels, and PL-1 (a) itself sends polity facts per seat through H13): the three channels are named.] No PL wave waits on them.] [CURED 2026-10-18 (fp-final r2) — SEAMS-r2-17: "the CROWN'S ROAD WARDENS" → "the crown's riders" (PR's R-8 struck `warden`: a landed role label, CH's display noun, EC's `route_wardenship`, the map's "wardens' terms"). SEAMS-r2-10: PL no longer co-signs a second summons kind for the same men (§4.1, OD-PL-50). RULINGS-ROUND2b HOST-r2-5 (the chair's error corrected): "opens H16" → the events window. SEAMS-r2-20 (routed to PR): the root's own read and the sub-vassal line are written here for PR to cite.]
